Tools: Rocq (formerly Coq)

- (Logic, Proof/Reason technique) A **logical argument** establishing the truth of a proposition.
- (Language feature/design, Programming paradigm, Formal system, Proof/Reason technique) In Rocq, a term of a propositional type constructed interactively via tactics or directly as a term. This draws from the ${fref("/01-programming-language-theory/02-concepts/curry-howard-correspondence.td")}.
